/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T13:29:45-08:00","id":1271237,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm pumped... And now I'm imagining &quot;legacy heroes&quot; like The Phantom as Changelings who pass on their title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T15:35:54-08:00","id":1271291,"title":"","content":"Is it a sign of how much of a nerd I am that my instant Entitlement idea is &quot;Grandmaster of Changeling Martial Arts&quot;?<br /> <br /> And then &quot;Symbol of Peace&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T17:07:48-08:00","id":1271332,"title":"","content":"I think it damages certain Eldrich Entitlements, which tended to be more global in Scope, like the Lost Pantheon, Knights if Widows Peak, the Black Apples, Office of the Vizeriers, and so on so the limit on the size of Legion Entitlements should not apply to Eldrich Entitlements.<br /> <br /> I also wish we'd gotten an example of the mechanics of both an Entitlement and Eldritch Entitlement so we have something more solid to discuss, we only have the basic concept, which is interesting, but hard to fully grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T17:48:15-08:00","id":1271344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271332#post1271332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it damages certain Eldrich Entitlements, which tended to be more global in Scope, like the Lost Pantheon, Knights if Widows Peak, the Black Apples, Office of the Vizeriers, and so on so the limit on the size of Legion Entitlements should not apply to Eldrich Entitlements.<br /> <br /> I also wish we'd gotten an example of the mechanics of both an Entitlement and Eldritch Entitlement so we have something more solid to discuss, we only have the basic concept, which is interesting, but hard to fully grasp.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of get this idea as it definitely requires a complete change in one's thinking of entitlements, but I don't think its ultimately problematic. It doesn't actually present the limitations as hard and fast, and its really the sort of thing that would be handled on a case by case basis. Lost Pantheon should be consistent with mythmaking tropes, but the Office of Vizerial Counsel is, in 1st ed canon, the legacy of a single changeling. And there are some non-eldritch orders who should probably be on the big side too if they are to remain in canon as an entitlement (legion of the iron wall.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: With the idea that non-seasonal courts are all over the place being true in 2e in spirit, if not in practice, some 1e entitlements would probably be better served as courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","user":"schizoPOP","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T20:38:14-08:00","id":1271368,"title":"","content":"I hope there's still some way to represent participation in larger Changeling groups.<br /> <br /> Though at the worst, you can always just make them through the Mystery Cults system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T21:57:34-08:00","id":1271375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271344#post1271344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sort of get this idea as it definitely requires a complete change in one's thinking of entitlements, but I don't think its ultimately problematic. It doesn't actually present the limitations as hard and fast, and its really the sort of thing that would be handled on a case by case basis. Lost Pantheon should be consistent with mythmaking tropes, but the Office of Vizerial Counsel is, in 1st ed canon, the legacy of a single changeling. And there are some non-eldritch orders who should probably be on the big side too if they are to remain in canon as an entitlement (legion of the iron wall.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: With the idea that non-seasonal courts are all over the place being true in 2e in spirit, if not in practice, some 1e entitlements would probably be better served as courts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which entitlements would you do as courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T21:59:30-08:00","id":1271376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271368#post1271368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope there's still some way to represent participation in larger Changeling groups.<br /> <br /> Though at the worst, you can always just make them through the Mystery Cults system.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think Mystery Cults have the right mechanics for some entitlement organizations.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if the 5th dot created an thematic Entitlement that fit the broader themes of the Mystery Cult, so the Mystery cult is the organization that ties all the different titles that fit it's theme together. Example the Lost Pantheon Mystery Cult, dots \u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 give various benefits, but the \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 dot grants an entitlement unique to the Character's role within the Pantheon, like one might be God of Thunder, another God of Lust, another Goddess of Dolphins, and another the Goddess of Screams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-28-2018, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T11:20:55-08:00","id":1271513,"title":"","content":"What about just handing out Influence (Whatever) at that dot, except they can spend Glamour instead of Essence/Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T15:31:37-08:00","id":1271604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271375#post1271375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which entitlements would you do as courts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solstice Court would seem an obvious choice, though if one wants to emphasize to the &quot;wannabe court&quot; angle it'd possibly be better off as a mystery cult. Other groups such as the Phantom Tongs (for whom being a nebulous organization is sort of the point), or the College of Worms (whose &quot;Let's study fate&quot; purview I don't think is specific to translate into a discrete role.) The Legion of the Iron Wall should probably be some sort of organization to remain recognizable, though it may possible to have a small set of Titles (Drill Sargent, Quartermaster, etc.) with buff and leadership focused effects. (Thereby making the beneficaries of their abilities the &quot;legion&quot; in an honorary sense.)<br /> <br /> Of course, in some cases the 1e entitlement could translate into both court and Title. (I.E. any number of members of the Toll-Taker court may gain glamour from hunting bounties but only one gets to be Boba Fett.)<br /> <br /> I don't think there's really magic formula here for what makes the best conversion. Probably should go with whatever seems the most interesting to the writer. (and 1e entitlements are already an eclectic grab bag of abilities so its hard to say one way or another from a purely logistical standpoint.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T15:54:51-08:00","id":1271607,"title":"","content":"The Margrave of the Brim remains, as always, the anti-court court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T16:40:15-08:00","id":1271612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271513#post1271513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about just handing out Influence (Whatever) at that dot, except they can spend Glamour instead of Essence/Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T20:42:14-08:00","id":1271680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271368#post1271368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope there's still some way to represent participation in larger Changeling groups.<br /> <br /> Though at the worst, you can always just make them through the Mystery Cults system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of Noble Orders that are basically Mystery Cults based on an Entitlement.<br /> <br /> There are many scarecrows in the Ministry, but only one Scarecrow Minister to lead them. Upon swearing their Oath to this secretive Noble Order, each initiate must give the Minister a mask that represents one of their own greatest fears. He hides each one in the gloomy thicket behind his seemingly dilapidated hollow. Any member who proves her worth to the Ministry is eventually invited to search for her mask and claim the newly hedge-forged token. One of these worthies may even dare to claim the title of Scarecrow Minister for herself someday. The current Minister hopes it's someday soon...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T23:21:27-08:00","id":1271710,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Expanding idea of 1E Noble Orders as Mystery Cults under 2E Title Bearer </span>- I would still makes that there is only one Entitled <b>in particular Freehold <i>and/or</i> local Hedge</b>. I still want's to make at least one Scarecrow Minister or Duchess of the Icebound Heart per chronicle setting, not traveling around the world just to find this particular Title Bearer now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Her 'acolytes' as Mystery Cults in region they are more than welcome.<br /> <br /> And as Freeholds are largely independent - and each of them fall in to their own, particular 'Great Story' - I can easily see that there can be only one Title Bearer in each only <b>this particular</b> 'Story' of Freehold. No need to roam the world if local upholder is in the Freehold. If there are no, then we talk about quest kind of storyline... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-29-2018, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T01:20:41-08:00","id":1271721,"title":"","content":"So, the new Entitlements are more like the equivalent of commoner titles, like Prince of Thieves or King of Fools: It may command some degree of importance and respect among the populace (goblins), but for the real nobility (True Fae) they are more or less laughable imitations of their titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T06:14:10-08:00","id":1271753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271721#post1271721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the new Entitlements are more like the equivalent of commoner titles, like Prince of Thieves or King of Fools: It may command some degree of importance and respect among the populace (goblins), but for the real nobility (True Fae) they are more or less laughable imitations of their titles.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, the Gentry take them far more serious then that, they seem to treat them almost like Gentry titles, viewing the bearer AS the title, instead of who they actually are as a person. So if a particular gentry had a bet going with the previous holder of the title, they expect the current holder to keep that bet and remember it. <br /> <br /> It's almost like the Gentry don't understand that Entitlements don't work like Gentry titles, that an Entitlement doesn't come with a living manifestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T07:28:52-08:00","id":1271768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271710#post1271710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Expanding idea of 1E Noble Orders as Mystery Cults under 2E Title Bearer </span>- I would still makes that there is only one Entitled <b>in particular Freehold <i>and/or</i> local Hedge</b>. I still want's to make at least one Scarecrow Minister or Duchess of the Icebound Heart per chronicle setting, not traveling around the world just to find this particular Title Bearer now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Her 'acolytes' as Mystery Cults in region they are more than welcome.<br /> <br /> And as Freeholds are largely independent - and each of them fall in to their own, particular 'Great Story' - I can easily see that there can be only one Title Bearer in each only <b>this particular</b> 'Story' of Freehold. No need to roam the world if local upholder is in the Freehold. If there are no, then we talk about quest kind of storyline... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually more in favor of each Entitlement being unique. While there may only be one Scarecrow Minister, keep in mind that he still has close ties to the Pumpkin King of Boston as well as the Queen of the Damned in New Orleans. Although they each have a different Entitlement, their Noble Orders basically perform the same function in their respective freeholds, so they share knowledge and information with each other. Then again, perhaps The Scarecrow Minister is the head of a far-reaching global organization and each freehold's congregation is led by a thematically Entitled member of his Ministry. I guess it just depends on what works better for your chronicle, but I really like each title being it's own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:03:24-08:00","id":1271819,"title":"","content":"I must say that the way Entitlements are presented kind of remind me of the mange &quot;Are You Alice?&quot;- I don't want to spoil (and it has been ages since I read it), but the principle of &quot;playing a role&quot; which grants you certain privileges as long as you stay in role, and take them from you once you defy it, while basing some sort of an erratic clauses and interactions which seem to be invented by someone mad at best, really do give that kind of vibe into it. It is funny that as 2e went all the way in order to detach from the &quot;Wyrd as a force of stories&quot; theme, while entitlements seem to bring it from the back door. You play a character in a story not your own in order to enjoy the benefits it grants you. Sure, you may want to stop taking part in the play- but doing so always require you to find a proper replacement, as the story still being told. You may act outside of your role, of course- you are still a being with free choice- but the story doesn't like it, and it may end up with some dire consequences. <br /> <br /> In a way, entitlements are the ultimate spit in the face of the Gentry- they tell their own stories, but are trapped and defined by them, unable to get out. Changelings are kidnapped and forced against their will to take part in those stories, unless they manage to get out. Entitlements is about living in the story of someone else, but choosing which story you live in, and which character you play. It is the ultimate victory over the True Fae- that you can make a choice they can not, and that you have the freedom they will never have.<br /> <br /> I think I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:12:18-08:00","id":1271823,"title":"","content":"Tell you one thing-the principle of this just made The Rosiere easier to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T13:35:32-08:00","id":1271837,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, Goblin Queen seem similar to an Entitlement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T15:02:35-08:00","id":1271854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271837#post1271837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, Goblin Queen seem similar to an Entitlement.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a question about whether the two are going to be conflated now or not.<br /> <br /> I hope not, and I even think not, but I can see the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T15:53:04-08:00","id":1271860,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong ofme to ponder that a quick way to found a new Entitlenent is to take/gain a Gentry's Title? Not became one of the Fair Folk, but to strip them of one their bulwarks as if you won it in a Fued.<br /> <br /> Gentry are just a bunch of Titles bound around a Name and technically a changeling can win one in a bet.<br /> <br /> Oops, now you are 'the Cruel Heart of the Glacier', time to use the Wyrd to bind it into something the Gentry can't take back; boom! Now the Duchy of the Icebound Heart is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T15:56:26-08:00","id":1271862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271860#post1271860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong ofme to ponder that a quick way to found a new Entitlenent is to take/gain a Gentry's Title? Not became one of the Fair Folk, but to strip them of one their bulwarks as if you won it in a Fued.<br /> <br /> Gentry are just a bunch of Titles bound around a Name and technically a changeling can win one in a bet.<br /> <br /> Oops, now you are 'the Cruel Heart of the Glacier', time to use the Wyrd to bind it into something the Gentry can't take back; boom! Now the Duchy of the Icebound Heart is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order for that to work, you'd have to have a Feud-promise for the Title, and with no Indulgence to win it on over, that'd be a tough order to obtain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T16:39:52-08:00","id":1271871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271837#post1271837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, Goblin Queen seem similar to an Entitlement.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1271854#post1271854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a question about whether the two are going to be conflated now or not.<br /> <br /> I hope not, and I even think not, but I can see the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably going to depend on what the actual mechanics that are tied to 2e Entitlements are. I won't have a hard time believing if its going to be based on Conditions, but who knows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T11:14:43-08:00","id":1272016,"title":"","content":"The idea is D.O.A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T13:51:58-08:00","id":1272037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1271113-entitlements-preview?p=1272016#post1272016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--b